  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Domestic Awardees Undisclosed obligated $374M in FY2026 to date. Domestic Awardees Undisclosed has 4,132 awards this fiscal year and an average award size of $90.5K. Obligations fell down 32.1% year over year. Agency for International Development is the dominant buyer, obligating $343M of the FY2026 total. Other Scientific and Technical Consulting Services is the largest market for Domestic Awardees Undisclosed with $273M in obligations, followed by All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services with $71.8M. Historical context shows variability: FY23 obligations were $1.1B and FY24 obligations were $1.3B, while FY25 obligations were $550M. The FY2026 to date total is partial for the fiscal year. Top buying agencies beyond Agency for International Development include the Department of the Treasury with $20.6M and the Department of Justice with $16.4M. Markets beyond consulting include Security Guards and Patrol Services at $16.4M and International Affairs at $14.4M. The dataset includes negative obligation figures for some agencies, which reduce the FY2026 total.",
